### In-Depth Study: Java Applet Architecture, Lifecycle, Graphics & <param> Tag

#### 1. Architectural Lifecycle of an Applet:
```
       +---------------------------------------------+
       |                   init()                    |
       |  (Initializes variables, fonts, components) |
       +---------------------------------------------+
                              |
                              v
       +---------------------------------------------+
       |                  start()                    |
       |     (Starts execution/threads; restarts)    |
       +---------------------------------------------+
                 |                         ^
                 | paint(Graphics g)       |
                 v                         |
       +-------------------+               |
       |  Active Execution |               | start()
       +-------------------+               |
                 |                         |
                 | Page navigated away     |
                 v                         |
       +---------------------------------------------+
       |                   stop()                    |
       |    (Pauses execution, stops worker loops)   |
       +---------------------------------------------+
                              |
                              | Browser closed
                              v
       +---------------------------------------------+
       |                  destroy()                  |
       |         (Final memory reclamation)          |
       +---------------------------------------------+
```

#### 2. Passing Parameters via the `<param>` Tag:
Applets read runtime configuration parameters embedded within enclosing HTML documents:
```html
<applet code="GraphicsApplet.class" width="400" height="300">
    <param name="bannerText" value="Mahatma Gandhi Institute of Technology">
    <param name="shapeRadius" value="80">
</applet>
```
Inside the applet's `init()` method, parameters are retrieved using:
```java
String text = getParameter("bannerText");
```

#### 3. Complete Demonstrative Java Implementation:
```java
import javax.swing.*;
import java.awt.*;

// Implemented using standard modern Swing JPanel component for execution in standalone and applet environments
public class GraphicsDrawingDemo extends JPanel {
    private String banner = "MGIT Autonomous Examination 2026";

    @Override
    protected void paintComponent(Graphics g) {
        super.paintComponent(g);

        Graphics2D g2d = (Graphics2D) g;
        g2d.setRenderingHint(RenderingHints.KEY_ANTIALIASING, RenderingHints.VALUE_ANTIALIAS_ON);

        // 1. Draw Title Text
        g2d.setFont(new Font("Arial", Font.BOLD, 16));
        g2d.setColor(new Color(30, 41, 59));
        g2d.drawString(banner, 40, 35);

        // 2. Draw Rectangle
        g2d.setColor(new Color(37, 99, 235)); // Accent Blue
        g2d.drawRect(50, 70, 150, 90);
        g2d.setColor(new Color(219, 234, 254));
        g2d.fillRect(51, 71, 149, 89);
        g2d.setColor(Color.BLACK);
        g2d.drawString("Rectangle", 90, 120);

        // 3. Draw Circle / Oval
        g2d.setColor(new Color(5, 150, 105)); // Accent Green
        g2d.drawOval(240, 70, 100, 100);
        g2d.setColor(new Color(209, 250, 229));
        g2d.fillOval(241, 71, 99, 99);
        g2d.setColor(Color.BLACK);
        g2d.drawString("Circle", 275, 125);
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        JFrame frame = new JFrame("Applet Graphics Simulation");
        frame.setDefaultCloseOperation(JFrame.EXIT_ON_CLOSE);
        frame.setSize(440, 260);
        frame.add(new GraphicsDrawingDemo());
        frame.setLocationRelativeTo(null);
        frame.setVisible(true);
    }
}
```

$$\therefore \text{Graphics primitive drawing combined with parameter tags enabled dynamic interactive browser visualizations.}$$
